@startuml
title POST /api/oslfs/create/prepare + /send — record a new OSLF document on chain
skinparam backgroundColor #F8FBFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #294C60
skinparam sequence {
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #EAF5FF
  ParticipantBorderColor #38789E
  LifeLineBorderColor #6A92AA
  GroupBackgroundColor #FFF3E8
  GroupBorderColor #D97638
}

actor "Document owner" as Owner #FFD8C2
participant "OslfsApiSdk\n.create(req)" as SDK #D5EAF7
participant "EmbersEvents\n(WebSocket)" as Events #E3D8F5
participant "Embers API" as API #FFC9A8
participant "OslfsService" as Domain #CDEACC
participant "F1r3node\nchain + observer" as Chain #FFE4A6

Owner -> SDK : create({ name, description?, query? })

group Phase 1 — prepare (deploys nothing; identities minted here)
SDK -> API : POST /api/oslfs/create/prepare
API -> Domain : prepare_create_contract
Domain -> Domain : mint id = UUIDv4,\nversion = UUIDv7;\nrender create.rho
Domain -> Chain : get head block index
Chain --> Domain : valid-after block number
Domain --> API : CreateOslfResp\n{ id, version, contract }
API --> SDK : PrepareResponse { response, token }
end

group Sign, subscribe, send
SDK -> SDK : signed = signContract(contract, privateKey)
SDK -> Events : subscribeForDeploy(\n  hex(signed.sig).toLowerCase(), maxWait)
SDK -> API : POST /api/oslfs/create/send\n{ prepare_request, prepare_response,\n  request: signed, token }
API -> API : verify the echo hash binding
API -> Domain : deploy signed contract
Domain -> Chain : deploy
Chain --> Domain : accepted
API <-- Domain : deploy id
SDK <-- API : 200 SendResp { deploy_id }
SDK --> Owner : { prepareResponse, sendResponse,\n  waitForFinalization }
end

group Finalization — observed on the WebSocket
Chain --> Events : Finalized { deploy_id, ...,\n  node_type: Observer }
Events --> Owner : waitForFinalization resolves\n(or rejects after maxWait)
end

note over Domain #FFF0C7
The document identity (UUIDv4 id) and its first
version (UUIDv7) exist from prepare onward, but
the record exists on chain only after the send's
deploy finalizes. An abandoned prepare leaves
nothing behind.
end note
@enduml
